\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. It fell upon a summer day,
\par When Jesus walked in Galilee,
\par The mothers from a village brought
\par Their children to His knee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He took them in His arms, and laid
\par His hands on each remembered head;
\par Suffer these little ones to come
\par To Me, He gently said.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Forbid them not; unless ye bear
\par The childlike heart your hearts within,
\par Unto My kingdom ye may come
\par But may not enter in.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Master, I fain would enter there;
\par O let me follow Thee, and share
\par Thy meek and lowly heart, and be
\par Freed from all worldly care.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Of innocence, and love, and trust,
\par Of quiet work, and simple word,
\par Of joy, and thoughtlessness of self,
\par Build up my life, good Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. All happy thoughts, and gentle ways,
\par And loving-kindness daily given,
\par And freedom through obedience gained,
\par Make in my heart Thy heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. All happy thus to live and move!
\par And sweet this world, where I shall find
\par God's beauty everywhere, His love,
\par His good in all mankind.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. Then, father, grant this childlike heart,
\par That I may come to Christ, and feel
\par His hands on me in blessing laid,
\par Love-giving, strong to heal.
\par                                 Amen.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

